---
import Post from "../../layouts/Post.astro";
import SleepNav from "../../components/SleepNav.astro";
import record from "../../data/sleep/record.json";
import { Content } from "../../data/sleep/notebook.md";
const latest = record.entries.at(-1);
const paired = record.entries.filter((entry) => entry.oura && entry.coros);
const latestOura = [...record.entries].reverse().find((entry) => entry.oura && entry.oura.score_eligible !== false);
const latestCoros = [...record.entries].reverse().find((entry) => entry.coros);
const frontmatter = { title: "Sleep performance", description: "An explicit pursuit of better sleep: goals, evidence, measurements, a daily record and the next frontier.", updated: record.updated };
---
<Post frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <SleepNav current="notebook" />
  <p>I want an explicit target to pursue. With running, the target is a score profile on the World Athletics tables. With food, improvement spans nutritional adequacy, taste, speed and cost. Sleep needs the same discipline: decide what matters, specify the measurement and target, improve, verify the result, then expand.</p>
  <p>The larger ambition is exceptional capability and a long life with that capability available. A sleep score can give the project a near-term benchmark. Research and functional measurements determine which broader claims the result supports.</p>
  <h2 id="present-position">Present position</h2>
  <div class="tablewrap"><table aria-label="Sleep project position"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Question</th><th scope="col">Current position</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row">Recorded evidence</th><td>{record.entries.length} dated entries, {paired.length} with data from both providers (including flagged incomplete recordings); latest ending <a href={`/sleep/record/#night-${latest?.id}`}>{latest?.wake_date}</a></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Device grading</th><td>{latestOura && <>Latest eligible Oura {latestOura.oura.score} on <a href={`/sleep/record/#night-${latestOura.id}`}>{latestOura.wake_date}</a>. </>}{latestCoros && <>Latest COROS {latestCoros.coros.sleep_score} on <a href={`/sleep/record/#night-${latestCoros.id}`}>{latestCoros.wake_date}</a>. </>}{latest?.oura?.score_eligible === false && <> Latest Oura {latest.oura.score} is from an incomplete recording and excluded from whole-night milestones.</>}{(!latest?.oura || !latest?.coros) && <>Latest entry has pending provider data; earlier grades are not assigned to it.</>}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">First target proposals</th><td><a href="/sleep/targets/#score-milestones">14-day average Oura score ≥85, then a 28-day average ≥90 with coverage and consistency requirements</a></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Personal physiological optimum</th><td>Not established; each metric has a separate <a href="/sleep/measurements/">interpretation and target status</a></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Next decision</th><td>{latest?.next_focus?.[0] ?? "Identify a meaningful limiting factor and a measurable outcome before selecting an intervention"}</td></tr>
  </tbody></table></div>
  <p><a href="/sleep/record/#recent-comparison">Compare the recent nights</a> · <a href="/sleep/research/personal-experiments/#the-current-routine-proposal">Routine proposal and follow-ups</a></p>
  <Content />
</Post>
